{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01G87cBxxLQpZtorQqabwbd8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have all the context. The `yes` command needs to handle the `--` separator for arguments. Looking at the test cases, I notice `yes` tests use `pipe_through: \"head -n N\"` — since `RunDiffTests` likely doesn't support piping natively, the tests need to wrap the binary invocation through a shell with `head`.\n\nLet me check how the existing `DiffTest` struct works — it's already provided in `package_contracts`. The `DiffTest` struct has `Args`, `Env`, `ExitCode` etc. but no `pipe_through` field. So the tests will need to use shell wrapping to pipe through `head`.\n\nLet me also check the `testutils` package to understand `BuildBinary`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7076,"cache_read_input_tokens":38381,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7076},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ecf39f2-e3af-4bf5-864a-659ffb740ed4","uuid":"cfbf9aaa-aa79-4993-a002-d4732e262a92"}
